# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sciencebouk — environment configuration guide
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There are three env files. Copy each matching .env.example to .env:
#
#   backend/.env    ← Django backend vars        (authoritative: backend/.env.example)
#   frontend/.env   ← Vite VITE_* vars           (authoritative: frontend/.env.example)
#   .env  (here)    ← optional shared overrides + docker-compose interpolation
#
# BACKEND LOAD PRECEDENCE
#   settings.py loads backend/.env FIRST, then this root .env, keeping the FIRST
#   occurrence of each key. So backend/.env WINS over this file. Put canonical
#   backend values in backend/.env; use this root .env only for shared overrides.
#
# LOCAL DEV — the short version
#   backend/.env :  DJANGO_DEBUG=1
#   frontend/.env:  (defaults work — API at http://localhost:8000/api)
#
# The full, commented variable lists with defaults live in the two per-tier
# .env.example files. Keep any keys you add here consistent with those.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── docker-compose interpolation only ────────────────────────────────────────
# These are NOT read by Django settings.py — they are substituted into the
# (gitignored) compose files. Safe to omit unless you run the Docker stack.
DOMAIN=example.com
DB_PASSWORD=generate-a-real-password
